END.TO-IB-s-7 BOUNDS, verbatim","statement":"A default tax setting is not client tax status."},{"applies_to":"benchmark","id":"NO_BENCHMARK_TEMPLATE_KEEPS_THE_CALCULATION_BENCHMARK","source":"IRPT_BCKEND.TO-IB-s-7 BOUNDS, verbatim","statement":"A No Benchmark template does not remove the calculation benchmark."}],"intake_controls":{"_ambiguous_symbols_note":"A symbol mapping to exactly ONE currency here is still NOT an establishment -- it is recorded so the SIGNAL is visible and a contradiction with an established code can be seen. The cell's law is that no symbol establishes a currency, and a one-entry list does not create an exception to it.","_iso_list_claim":"recorded, NOT exhaustive -- ISO 4217 carries ~180 active codes. A code outside this list reads as NOT-AN-ISO-TOKEN, which sends the row to AMBIGUOUS/UNDECLARED rather than to a wrong currency. The list is a RECOGNISER, and a recogniser that fails closed is safe to shorten; it is never used to decide that something IS a supported currency without `supported_currencies` agreeing.","_meta":{"author":"0.9.0_WK_IRPT_BCKEND~3 on IRPT_BCKEND.TO-IB-rt-11","cell":"IB-rt-11 (PRD row B7, CTO ruling 7, slug row C-S74)","law":"A value whose currency cannot be ESTABLISHED from the document is QUARANTINED, never relabeled to the expected one. A quarantine is a legitimate, reportable outcome -- not a failure to handle the case.","purpose":"THE CURRENCY AND UNIT POLICY, AS DATA. A supported-currency set that lives as a constant inside parse.py is a policy nobody can review or diff, and this one is the hinge of the cell's law: QUARANTINE OVER RELABELING.","why_this_is_a_SEPARATE_TOP_LEVEL_KEY":"`settings.settings` is a build input of irpt-ycharts-generate and its seven members are read by name there (recipe.SETTING_TO_VENDOR_FIELD). Adding an eighth member would put an intake policy into a vendor settings read-back. This key is a sibling, so that consumer's denominator of 7 is untouched."},"ambiguous_symbols":{"$":["USD","CAD","AUD","NZD","HKD","SGD","MXN","ARS","CLP","COP","UYU"],"A$":["AUD"],"C$":["CAD"],"CA$":["CAD"],"US$":["USD"],"£":["GBP","GIP","FKP","SHP"],"¥":["JPY","CNY"],"€":["EUR"]},"coordinates_NOT_inspected_STATED_AS_A_BLIND_SPOT":[{"coordinate":"WORKBOOK_OR_SHEET_LEVEL_NOTE","why":"a currency declared in a free-text note, a header/footer, a merged title cell or a separate cover sheet is not read by this parser. A specimen whose ONLY currency declaration lives there reads UNDECLARED, and UNDECLARED makes no currency claim at all -- so it is not relabeled, but it is also not caught."},{"coordinate":"CSV_SIDECAR_OR_FILENAME","why":"a filename such as HOLDINGS_CAD.csv is not a document declaration and is deliberately not read."}],"coordinates_inspected_that_never_ESTABLISH":[{"coordinate":"VALUE_CELL_TEXT","what_is_read":"the verbatim text of the value cell, before any symbol is stripped","why_it_cannot_establish":"a currency SYMBOL is ambiguous across currencies and the cell's law forbids inferring from one. It is recorded as a SIGNAL so a contradiction with an established code is visible, and a symbol with no establishing code elsewhere yields AMBIGUOUS_CURRENCY."}],"currency_is_ESTABLISHED_only_by":[{"coordinate":"DECLARED_CURRENCY_COLUMN","establishes_when":"the cell is a whole-token ISO-4217 alphabetic code","what_is_read":"the cell of a column whose header is one of the declared currency headers, on the SAME row as the value"},{"coordinate":"VALUE_COLUMN_HEADER","establishes_when":"the header carries a whole-token ISO-4217 alphabetic code (e.g. 'Market Value (CAD)'); the header's VOCABULARY ('Market Value', 'Amount') establishes nothing","what_is_read":"the header text of the column the number was read from"},{"coordinate":"XLSX_NUMBER_FORMAT","establishes_when":"the format code carries a whole-token ISO-4217 code, e.g. [$CAD]. A bare symbol (\"$\"#,##0.00) or a locale id ([$$-409]) establishes NOTHING -- a locale is not a currency declaration.","what_is_read":"the cell's own numFmt format code, resolved through xl/styles.xml cellXfs"}],"denominator":{"declared_blind_spot_coordinates":2,"establishing_coordinates":3,"inspected_non_establishing_coordinates":1,"supported_currencies":1},"iso4217_alphabetic_codes_recognised":["AUD","BRL","CAD","CHF","CNY","DKK","EUR","GBP","HKD","ILS","INR","JPY","KRW","MXN","NOK","NZD","SEK","SGD","TWD","USD","ZAR"],"supported_currencies":["USD"]},"settings":{"benchmark":{"caution":"A 'NO BENCHMARK' TEMPLATE DOES NOT REMOVE THE CALCULATION BENCHMARK. The three report templates the brief names are 'Comprehensive Overview (No Benchmark)', 'Comprehensive Comparison (No Benchmark)' and 'Comprehensive Multi-Comp (No Benchmark)'. 'No Benchmark' describes what the report DISPLAYS; the calculation still resolves a benchmark, and ^SPXTR is it. Reading the template name as 'there is no benchmark' would make every benchmark-relative number in the output unattributable.","claim":"recorded","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), '^SPXTR'","value":"^SPXTR"},"level_as_of_type":{"claim":"recorded","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), 'prior close'","value":"PRIOR_CLOSE"},"management_fee":{"claim":"recorded","display":"0.30% annual","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7) and the CRO brief section O3 @62301f71e0: 'The annual advisory fee is 0.30%, as specified in the newer workflow.'","supersedes":{"value":0.01,"when":"the July 2026 workflow","why_kept":"The superseded value is recorded BESIDE the current one rather than deleted. A reader who finds 0.01 in an older artifact needs to be able to tell 'historical' from 'someone changed it and did not say', and a file that carries only the current value cannot answer that."},"units":"ANNUAL_DECIMAL_FRACTION","value":0.003},"rebalance_frequency":{"claim":"recorded","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), 'quarterly rebalancing'","value":"QUARTERLY"},"reinvest_dividends":{"claim":"recorded","note":"FALSE is a CHOICE here, not an absence. A consumer that treats a missing key as false would reach the same behaviour for the wrong reason, which is why the key is present and explicit.","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), 'dividends false'","value":false},"start_of_series":{"claim":"recorded","note":"Oldest AVAILABLE is a property of the securities in the portfolio, so the concrete start date differs per request and is a vendor-returned fact, never a value this file can carry.","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), 'oldest start'","value":"OLDEST_AVAILABLE"},"tax_status":{"caution":"A DEFAULT TAX SETTING IS NOT A CLIENT'S TAX STATUS. This value is what the workflow's report configuration is set to; it says nothing about whether a given client's accounts are qualified or non-qualified. A cell that reads this and labels a client's output 'non-qualified' has converted a report setting into a claim about the client's tax situation, which is a statement Opal did not make.","claim":"recorded","source":"IRPT_BCKEND decomposition v0.1.1 s.2 (cell IB-s-7), 'non-qualified'","value":"NON_QUALIFIED"}}}}